<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prince Eugene of Savoy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1663">1663</a>–<a href="/years/1736">1736</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Eugene of Savoy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prince Eugene of Savoy was a Paris-born general in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> service and one of the greatest commanders of his age. He defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> at Zenta in 1697, shared victory with Marlborough at Blenheim in 1704 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>, and in the war of 1716 to 1718 won at Petrovaradin, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timisoara">Temeswar</a> and captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a>. His campaigns secured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banat">Banat</a> for the Habsburg monarchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prince-eugene-of-savoy.jpg" alt="Prince Eugene of Savoy" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacob van Schuppen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prinz_Eugene_of_Savoy.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
